==Russian==

===Etymology===
{{root|ru|ine-pro|*weyd-}}
{{bor+|ru|fr|guide}}. Ultimately from {{der|ru|ine-pro|*weyd-}} (via {{der|ru|gem-pro|*wītaną}}).

===Pronunciation===
* {{ru-IPA}}
* {{audio|ru|Ru-гид.ogg}}

===Noun===
{{ru-noun+|a=an}}

# [[guide]] {{gloss|someone who guides, especially someone hired to show people around a place}}

====Usage notes====
Russian has two terms corresponding to [[tour guide]]: {{m|ru|гид}} and {{m|ru|экскурсово́д}}. These are partially synonymous, but have different accents:
* {{m|ru|гид}} is usually a generalist, offering tours for a variety of museums and locations of interest;
* {{m|ru|экскурсово́д}} is usually a knowledgeable specialist, working at only one specific museum.

